 ( 12... b5 13. b4 { leaves the pawn on c6 weak, which encourages White to play for e3-e4. In the event of } e4 { White plays } 14. f3 exf3 15. Qxf3 $14 { with good chances on the light squares. } ) 
13. b4 ( { Now } 13. f3 $2 exf3 14. Qxf3 { is well met by } Nf8 { intending ...Ne6-g5. } ) 
axb4 14. axb4 Nf8 15. b5 Ne6 $13 { Black has two major choices to make. Should he castle or keep the rook on the h-file? And should the knight go to g5 quickly, or wait until ...g6-g5-g4 has been played? These decisions are beyond the scope of the exercise; but in any case, White is not playing on the queenside for free. } 
